From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 15:17:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: tell FEX of an executable view of a plain section on
 iOS

FEX decodes guest code only inside its executable intervals. The ARM64EC
NtMapViewOfSection wrappers notify it of an image's view, and nothing
else: a view of a plain section mapped executable (no NtProtectVirtualMemory
after it) never reached FEX. World of Warcraft's x64 client maps a
pagefile section twice, read-write and read-execute, writes its code
through the first and calls into the second: FEX decoded NOEXEC at the
first instruction there, raised NoExecOp, and Wow_loader.dll's
initialisation died with c0000005 (run 20261101T151452).

notify_map_view_of_section now passes an executable view of a section
that is not an image to FEX's NotifyMemoryProtect as the protection
change it is, and returns. An image's view goes on as before.

Linear: PLA-516
Class: upstream-bug
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-11-01-wow-x64-fex.md
Offered-upstream: not yet; upstream notifies an image's view only, as here before
---
 dlls/ntdll/signal_arm64ec.c | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/signal_arm64ec.c b/dlls/ntdll/signal_arm64ec.c
index cca4fddde13..fe73b7649b6 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/signal_arm64ec.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/signal_arm64ec.c
@@ -1943,6 +1943,23 @@ static void notify_map_view_of_section( HANDLE handle, void *addr, SIZE_T size,
         }
     }
     if (!pNotifyMapViewOfSection) return;
+    /* Playport (PLA-516, decision 0177): a view of a plain section mapped
+     * executable is guest code too. FEX decodes only what its executable
+     * intervals cover, and only an image's view reaches it below, so World of
+     * Warcraft's x64 client, which maps a pagefile section read-execute and
+     * writes its code through a second, read-write view, decoded NOEXEC at the
+     * first instruction there. Such a view is told to FEX as the protection
+     * change it is; an image's view goes on as before. */
+    if ((protect & (PAGE_EXECUTE | PAGE_EXECUTE_READ | PAGE_EXECUTE_READWRITE | PAGE_EXECUTE_WRITECOPY))
+        && pNotifyMemoryProtect && NtQuerySection( handle, SectionImageInformation, &info, sizeof(info), NULL ))
+    {
+        static int exec_views;
+        if (exec_views < 20)
+        { exec_views++; ERR( "[map-notify] executable view of a plain section addr=%p size=%p prot=%x: told to FEX\n",
+                             addr, (void *)size, protect ); }
+        pNotifyMemoryProtect( addr, size, protect, TRUE, STATUS_SUCCESS );
+        return;
+    }
     if (!NtCurrentTeb()->Tib.ArbitraryUserPointer)
     {
         static int skip_aup;
-- 
2.56.0

